        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<div class="resources_card"><div data-animate="slide-in" data-clip-sq="tl tr bl br" class="resources_card-visual-w" style=""><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6a5f29615015defef7c9471f/6a9d37d14ba1151be4327945_blog%20act%20research.png" loading="lazy" alt="" class="img_abs is-resources"></div><div class="resources_card-text"><div class="heading-with-p is-16 is-left is-grow"><div class="heading-with-p is-8 is-left"><div class="heading-with-p is-6 is-left"><div data-animate="slide-in" style="background-color: rgb(12, 91, 57); color: rgb(250, 250, 249);" class="resources_tag"><div fs-list-field="category">Research</div></div><h3 fs-list-field="title" data-animate="slide-in" class="heading-style-h4 text-weight-normal" style="">One Query on Amazon Athena Returned 43 Other AWS Accounts' SQL</h3></div><p fs-list-field="description" data-animate="slide-in" class="text-body text-style-2lines" style="">One extra field on an Athena API call returned the full text of SQL queries that other AWS accounts had just run, along with the account IDs that ran them. No query results came back, but statement text carries filter values, inserted rows and table structure. We reported it to AWS on 6 August 2026 and they closed it globally in four days. No customer action is required.</p></div><div data-animate="slide-in" class="resources_author-w" style=""><div fs-list-field="author" class="text-caption text-color-grey-medium">Oren Yomtov</div><div fs-list-field="date" class="text-caption text-color-disabled-grey">September 6, 2026</div></div></div></div><a aria-label="Read more" href="/resources/reading-other-aws-accounts-sql-on-amazon-athena" class="link_abs w-inline-block"></a></div>]]></content>
